Package: libfprint-goodix-spi
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
 fprintd (>= 1.94),
 systemd,
 udev,
Description: Goodix GDIX51C0 SPI driver for libfprint (shadow install)
 Out-of-tree libfprint driver for the Goodix GDIX51C0 host-processing
 fingerprint sensor, including the native ChicagoHS biometric backend
 (calibration, preprocessing, enrollment, matching and adaptive learning).
 .
 Following the upstream installer, this package does not replace the
 distribution libfprint. A patched libfprint and a patched fprintd are
 installed as a private "shadow" pair below /opt/goodix-spi-driver; a systemd
 drop-in for fprintd.service puts that library directory on LD_LIBRARY_PATH
 and starts the shadow daemon instead of the distribution one. The sensor is
 made visible through a udev rule for its ACPI modalias.
 .
 Uninstalling the package does not delete the on-disk sensor key, sensor
 calibration or enrolled fingerprints; see /usr/share/doc/libfprint-goodix-spi/
 README.Debian for the paths and for the manual cleanup procedure.
